cells:
  - kind: 1
    value: >
      # One-class SVM: source-data checks


      These checks inspect BOMEN_TREES before building an anomaly model. Results

      below are the observed outputs supplied on 28 October 2026. 


      Candidate question: Which trees have unusual recorded age and
      trunk-diameter

      combinations compared with trees of the same species, and where are they?

      A flag means review the record; it is not a diagnosis of tree health.
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: |
      ## 1. Confirm source columns
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: |
      SELECT column_name, data_type, data_type_owner
      FROM user_tab_columns
      WHERE table_name = 'BOMEN_TREES'
      ORDER BY column_id;

      -- COLUMN_NAME                   DATA_TYPE    DATA_TYPE_OWNER
      -- ----------------------------- ------------ ---------------
      -- SOURCE_TREE_NUMBER            NUMBER       null
      -- SPECIES_COMMON_NAME           VARCHAR2     null
      -- SRT_WETENS                    VARCHAR2     null
      -- TREE_AGE                      NUMBER       null
      -- AGE_CLASS_CATEGORY            VARCHAR2     null
      -- TRUNK_DIAMETER                VARCHAR2     null
      -- OWNER                         VARCHAR2     null
      -- MANAGER                       VARCHAR2     null
      -- PRUNING_FORM                  VARCHAR2     null
      -- MONUMENTAL_FIELD              VARCHAR2     null
      -- SOURCE_WORK_PACKAGE_CODE      VARCHAR2     null
      -- SOURCE_WORK_PACKAGE           VARCHAR2     null
      -- GROWING_SITE                  VARCHAR2     null
      -- STREET_NAME                   VARCHAR2     null
      -- CITY_DISTRICT                 VARCHAR2     null
      -- COUNTER                       NUMBER       null
      -- SOURCE_RECORD_ID              NUMBER       null
      -- DISTRICT_NAME                 VARCHAR2     null
      -- NEIGHBOURHOOD                 VARCHAR2     null
      -- WGS84_LONGITUDE               NUMBER       null
      -- WGS84_LATITUDE                NUMBER       null
      -- SOURCE_PROJECTED_X_COORDINATE NUMBER       null
      -- SOURCE_PROJECTED_Y_COORDINATE NUMBER       null
      -- SOURCE_TEXT_IEPVAK_OMS        VARCHAR2     null
      -- SOURCE_CODE_PKBZ              VARCHAR2     null
      -- GEOMETRY                      SDO_GEOMETRY MDSYS
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: |
      ## 2. Check diameter classes

      TRUNK_DIAMETER is a category, not a measured numeric diameter. 
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: |
      SELECT TRUNK_DIAMETER, COUNT(*) AS TREE_COUNT
      FROM BOMEN_TREES
      GROUP BY TRUNK_DIAMETER
      ORDER BY TREE_COUNT DESC
      FETCH FIRST 20 ROWS ONLY;

      -- TRUNK_DIAMETER TREE_COUNT
      -- -------------- ----------
      -- 25-50 cm            61446
      -- 10-25 cm            44603
      -- 0-10 cm             27782
      -- 50-75 cm            12304
      -- 75-100 cm            2236
      -- >100 cm               680
      -- (null)                 23
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: |
      ## 3. Check species coverage and missing inputs
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: |
      SELECT SRT_WETENS AS SPECIES,
             COUNT(*) AS TREES,
             COUNT(TREE_AGE) AS WITH_AGE,
             COUNT(TRUNK_DIAMETER) AS WITH_DIAMETER
      FROM BOMEN_TREES
      GROUP BY SRT_WETENS
      ORDER BY TREES DESC
      FETCH FIRST 20 ROWS ONLY;

      -- SPECIES                              TREES WITH_AGE WITH_DIAMETER
      -- ------------------------------------ ----- -------- -------------
      -- Quercus robur                         8068     8068          8066
      -- Alnus glutinosa                       5773     5773          5769
      -- Tilia x europaea                      4851     4851          4851
      -- Platanus x hispanica                  3762     3762          3762
      -- Fraxinus excelsior                    3703     3703          3702
      -- Salix alba                            3342     3342          3342
      -- Tilia x europaea 'Pallida'            3323     3323          3323
      -- Acer pseudoplatanus                   3152     3152          3151
      -- Fraxinus excelsior 'Westhofs Glorie'  3000     3000          3000
      -- Ulmus 'Lobel'                         2843     2843          2843
      -- Fagus sylvatica                       2799     2799          2799
      -- Robinia pseudoacacia 'Bessoniana'     2595     2595          2595
      -- Ulmus hollandica 'Groeneveld'         2573     2573          2573
      -- Pyrus calleryana 'Chanticleer'        2298     2298          2298
      -- Ulmus 'Clusius'                       2116     2116          2116
      -- Prunus avium 'Plena'                  2019     2019          2019
      -- Acer pseudoplatanus 'Erectum'         1812     1812          1812
      -- Acer campestre                        1787     1787          1786
      -- Alnus x spaethii 'Spaeth'             1724     1724          1724
      -- Tilia x europaea 'Euchlora'           1649     1649          1649
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: |
      ## 4. Verify unique case IDs and age range
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: |
      SELECT COUNT(*) AS TREES,
             COUNT(DISTINCT SOURCE_RECORD_ID) AS UNIQUE_IDS,
             MIN(TREE_AGE) AS MIN_AGE,
             MAX(TREE_AGE) AS MAX_AGE,
             SUM(CASE WHEN SRT_WETENS IS NULL
                        OR TREE_AGE IS NULL
                        OR TRUNK_DIAMETER IS NULL
                      THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS INCOMPLETE_ROWS
      FROM BOMEN_TREES;

      -- TREES UNIQUE_IDS MIN_AGE MAX_AGE INCOMPLETE_ROWS
      -- ------ ---------- ------- ------- ---------------
      -- 149074     149074       0    1016              27
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: |
      ## 5. Inspect the oldest recorded trees
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: |
      SELECT SOURCE_RECORD_ID, SRT_WETENS, TREE_AGE, TRUNK_DIAMETER
      FROM BOMEN_TREES
      WHERE TREE_AGE >= 300
      ORDER BY TREE_AGE DESC
      FETCH FIRST 20 ROWS ONLY;

      -- SOURCE_RECORD_ID SRT_WETENS                  TREE_AGE TRUNK_DIAMETER
      -- ---------------- --------------------------- -------- --------------
      --          1431948 Ulmus resista 'New Horizon'     1016 10-25 cm
      --          1424283 Pyrus communis 'Juttepeer'       384 75-100 cm
      --          1322978 Quercus robur                    326 50-75 cm
      --          1376278 Quercus robur                    303 >100 cm
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: |
      ## 6. Compare numeric ages with age classes
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: |
      SELECT AGE_CLASS_CATEGORY,
             COUNT(*) AS TREES,
             MIN(TREE_AGE) AS MIN_AGE,
             MAX(TREE_AGE) AS MAX_AGE
      FROM BOMEN_TREES
      GROUP BY AGE_CLASS_CATEGORY
      ORDER BY TREES DESC;

      -- AGE_CLASS_CATEGORY TREES MIN_AGE MAX_AGE
      -- ------------------ ----- ------- -------
      -- Volwassen          81258      21    1016
      -- Halfwas            38529      11      30
      -- Jong               29283       0      15
      -- (null)                 4      65     100
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: |
      ## 7. Size the per-species model population
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      SELECT COUNT(*) AS SPECIES,
             SUM(CASE WHEN TREES >= 100 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS SPECIES_WITH_100_PLUS,
             SUM(CASE WHEN TREES < 100 THEN TREES ELSE 0 END) AS TREES_IN_SMALL_SPECIES
      FROM (
          SELECT SRT_WETENS, COUNT(*) AS TREES
          FROM BOMEN_TREES
          WHERE SRT_WETENS IS NOT NULL
            AND TREE_AGE IS NOT NULL
            AND TRUNK_DIAMETER IS NOT NULL
          GROUP BY SRT_WETENS
      );


      -- SPECIES SPECIES_WITH_100_PLUS TREES_IN_SMALL_SPECIES

      -- ------- --------------------- ----------------------

      --    1148                   203                  15405
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: >
      ## Model-design notes


      - First pilot species: Quercus robur (8,066 complete age/diameter rows).

      - Species with fewer than 100 complete records need an explicit
        "insufficient comparison data" outcome, not an automatic normal flag.
      - The 1,016-year record is a review candidate, not a health diagnosis.

      - BOMEN_TREES has no update timestamp. Saved model results need an
      explicit
        source-change check before reuse; row count alone cannot detect edits.
      - This notebook performs checks only. It does not create models, tables,
        views, agents, or map layers.
    languageId: markdown
